{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/616767-what-happens-when-the-gauntlet-is-thin","id":616767,"title":"What happens when the Gauntlet is thin?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-05T13:27:37-07:00","id":616767,"title":"What happens when the Gauntlet is thin?","content":"In the Dream Speaker book there is a Linear Magic path that allows Static Shamans to lower the Gauntlet. Remembering how the Ratkin became Wyld tainted by staying too long in the Umbra, what happens if the Gauntlet is reduced to a Rating of 2 or even 1? Or perhaps it's even turned into a Shallowing for an hour once or twice a day. What is going to be the effect on the material world and those living around it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T13:44:14-07:00","id":616787,"title":"","content":"Ratkin don't become Wyld-tainted from staying in the Umbra, they, like anyone else, undergo Disconnection from the physical, or at least risk it on such long trips. They become Wyld-tainted by listening to the maddened voice of the Rat God over Mother Rat.<br /> <br /> As to the actual question about low Gauntlet ratings, people feel spooked and often might be able to see hints of the Penumbra. There's a greater chance for more spirits to materialize, as well, since they can only do this with a Gnosis rating equal to or higher than the local Gauntlet. This is distinct from actually merging the two worlds in this location, which typically requires a lot more work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T14:46:45-07:00","id":616812,"title":"","content":"But does more Gnosis go through both ways? The Umbra is more nourished by the closer contact with the physical world and it should be easier to get Gnosis by meditating?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T14:49:00-07:00","id":616814,"title":"","content":"Also, don't Garou talk about the horrors of getting caught in the Gauntlet and describe it as the way Gaia feels?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T20:20:33-07:00","id":617102,"title":"","content":"Mercurial: I am... perplexed... by what exactly it is that you're trying to address, because it's stuff that's largely covered in various books (WW and M). The whole reason why Garou protect Caerns (which are often -- not always, but often -- just highly flavored Nodes/Crays, in Mage terms) is precisely because the Gauntlet *is* naturally thinner there -- there's no clarification required as to *why* that is &quot;a good thing&quot;, vis-a-vis having the Gauntlet be lower *elsewhere*. (Important sidenote: you've got the &quot;physical world nourishing the umbra&quot; slightly backwards -- it's the other way around. While penumbral realms -- and many deeper realms of the various umbrae -- are often reflections of the physical world, it is the spiritual power coming *from* the umbra that empowers the *physical* world, not the other way around. The channeling of gnosis by werewolves -- and quintessence by some mages -- into a caern/node/cray is to help support/strengthen the *caern*, not the umbra(e) that the said caern may lead/be linked to. That is an important metaphysical distinction... various Horizon Realms may require Gnosis/Quintessence, but that is because the mystical torque being applied there is altering the nature of &quot;x&quot; to suit the needs of the mages/whomever in question -- there is *plenty* of spiritual power out there in the various Realms beyond Earth... it just doesn't often have the pure Quintessence that *mages* require for fueling/performing &quot;x&quot;....) Having the Gauntlet be lowered to 2 or 1 allows for spirits to manifest into the physical world (or physical being in the penumbra to return to the physical world, if they have no other ability to do so once on &quot;the other side of the mirror&quot;) without the need for possessing the Materialize charm (or Embody, for wraiths/similar Low-Umbral entities). That's about it. Having it become a caern/node, proper, would entail either considerable ritual (detailed elsewhere) for the Garou to do it, or Prime:5 (along with at least Spirit:4, in this specific case) for a mage to create said caern.<br /> <br /> As far as getting caught in the Gauntlet being &quot;the way Gaia feels&quot; -- well, <i>yeah, </i>of course that's how she feels. The Gauntlet, as it currently (meaning the past millennia) exists, is a separation of Gaia's spirit from her physical embodiment with the side-effect of her often feeling cocooned and/or stuck in a web. This is how a werewolf (or anyone) feels when they get &quot;stuck&quot; crossing though the Gauntlet. I don't see where that has any bearing, directly, on the subject at hand, because there aren't enough Garou shamans in the *world* to shift the Gauntlet by any sustainable degree, and not all the Dreamspeakers backed by all the houses of Hermes and some high Ecstactics can hope to overcome the Paradox necessary to lower the Gauntlet in any meaningful way that would make Gaia &quot;feel better&quot;. So again, why even bring that up?<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, but to answer one point more specifically, vis-a-vis what would happen if the Gauntlet in an area were lowered to 2 or less (or occasionally Shallowing, now and again): spiritual manifestations would increase and the general locality would get a reputation for being &quot;weird&quot;, &quot;haunted&quot;, &quot;spooky&quot; and similar. (That's what happens, for examples, in some Haunts when the Shroud gets low enough that Embodying becomes child's play, or use of Outrage/Pandemonium becomes absurdly easy -- everybody avoids the &quot;haunted house at the top of the hill&quot;... except for the occasional kids who venture in on a dare... and their bodies are found later on in most... &quot;unnatural&quot;... states/poses of decay...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":1433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","user":"Just John, Forever...","date":".  spacing, cut/paste error 08-05-2015, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T23:13:09-07:00","id":617173,"title":"","content":"I've been pondering things like how the heart of the Wyld Caern in New York is supposed to be a place of inspiration, and I am curious what kind of motive a small circle of Verbena and Dream Speakers, and a LOT of static magicians, who have built a shrine to the Etheral Wind, would have to maintain a small place out in the woods, or even in the back alleys of a city, in keeping the Gauntlet constantly low. I figure that if asked, they would explain they are helping to create a healthier spirit world by allowing the cosmic air to flow back and forth, allowing Gaia to inhale and exhale, more easily in their part of the woods. The place would be strange, but I suspect that the spirits might be stronger there, depending on the sort of rituals and offerings made on a daily basis to the spirits there. This is actually for a fanfiction that I am writing. I am simply trying to confirm that the people who are doing this have a sound reason in thinking that they are helping to save the world by constantly paying homage to the Etheral Wind while trying to promote a spiritually and physically healthy environment. My inspiration is largely taken from Fort Condor in FFVII. The whole narrative of creating a bridge between this world and the next falls apart if there isn't a compelling reason for their efforts that don't make the people seem sympathetic and their work important.<br /> <br /> FYI, the antagonists in this game will be a Weaver strike team. The protagonists have to figure out a way to keep the place off of the Weaver's radar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 08-06-2015, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T03:05:21-07:00","id":617422,"title":"","content":"Usually the gauntlets mother offers seconds and informs it of its present state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}